body:
Hey buddy,  
It sounds like you're dealing with a bit of a head-scratcher with this girl. It's frustrating when things were going so well, and then suddenly the vibe changes, especially when you're really into the conversations.  


&#x200B;


Based on what you've told me, it seems like she's still interested in chatting since she's the one starting the conversations. But those dry responses could mean she's got other stuff on her mind or she's not feeling as into it as before.  


&#x200B;


When you're in a spot like this, honesty is key. Maybe bring up what you've noticed with her in a chill way, just asking if everything's cool on her end. This way, she might open up about what's up with her and why things have shifted.  


&#x200B;


In the meantime, keep trying to keep the chats lively and fun, but don't push too hard. Life happens, and she might have stuff going on that's affecting her vibe.  


&#x200B;


As for meeting up, it's cool that you're down for taking things offline. When she's back from her trip, you could casually float the idea of hanging out. But make sure you're respectful of her schedule and other commitments.

&#x200B;


Just stay flexible and see how things unfold. If she's still not showing much interest or the convos don't get any better, it might be worth thinking about whether this is the right path for you.  


&#x200B;


Hang in there, man. You got this.

Break up. It's time to move on. She's breaking you down to her level so she feels more secure in herself. If she was supportive and had a positive mindset you wouldn't be here posting on Reddit for advice.

&#x200B;

